```go
// line 880
if len(filesTouchedBefore) == 0 && state.Phase.IsActive() && state.TranscriptPath != "" {
    filesTouchedBefore = s.extractFilesFromLiveTranscript(ctx, state)
}
```

Are you suggesting: for ACTIVE sessions, **always** merge transcript-extracted files into `filesTouchedBefore`, not just when it's empty? That way the mid-turn files the agent wrote (but SaveStep hasn't recorded yet) would show up in the overlap check.

Or are you suggesting something different — parsing at actual read-back time (when querying checkpoint data) rather than at PostCommit time?

